# Engineering quality
- Determine actual dependency/config state before inventing commands or adding a framework.
- Preserve backward compatibility unless an ADR explicitly authorizes breaking changes.
- No prod changes; use migrations, staging fixtures and rollback plans.
- Never copy user-specific tokens or private Telegram identifiers into tests or output logs.
- Run relevant focused tests; report exactly which checks passed/failed/not executed.
